---
title: Document templates
description: Design your documents, with an AI or by hand.
---

nullish comes with clean default templates in English, German, French and Italian. When you want documents that look like you, design your own: the whole page is yours, not just a logo and a line of text.

Templates are made with the [nullish document templates](https://github.com/usenullish/document-templates) project. It shows a live preview of your documents with sample data, so you see every change right away. You can let an AI do the work or edit the templates yourself.

## Get the project

{% steps %}

1. Fork [usenullish/document-templates](https://github.com/usenullish/document-templates) on GitHub if you want to keep your templates in your own repository, then clone it:

   ```sh
   git clone https://github.com/usenullish/document-templates.git
   cd document-templates
   npm ci
   ```

2. Start the preview and open [localhost:4321](http://localhost:4321):

   ```sh
   npm run dev
   ```

{% /steps %}

## Design it with an AI

Open the project in a coding assistant such as Claude Code, Cursor or Copilot, and describe what you want:

- "Use my logo from `logo.svg` in the top left corner and our brand color `#1d4ed8` for the headings."
- "Put our address in the footer and the bank details next to the totals."
- "Make it look more like this PDF" (with an old invoice attached).

The project describes the data of every document, so the assistant knows what it can use. Keep the preview open next to it and ask for adjustments until it looks right.

## Or edit it yourself

Each document has its own folder in `src/templates/`. For invoices, it's `src/templates/invoices/`:

- `Invoice.astro` is the layout: what appears on the page, and where.
- `i18n.json` holds the texts in English, French, German and Italian.

Style it with plain CSS or Tailwind classes. Sizes are in millimeters, like on paper. The [project's README](https://github.com/usenullish/document-templates#readme) lists the data of every document and the template syntax.

{% aside %}
nullish only stores the HTML, so the template can't load anything from elsewhere. Embed your logo
as SVG or as a `data:` URI, and do the same for a custom font.
{% /aside %}

## Upload it to nullish

{% steps %}

1. Build the templates:

   ```sh
   npm run build
   ```

   You get one file per language for each document, e.g. in `templates/invoices/`: `en.html`, `fr.html`, `de.html` and `it.html`.

2. In nullish, go to **Settings → Billing → Document templates** and create a template. Give it a **Name**.

3. Choose **Add content** for each language you need: pick the **Language** and upload the matching file, e.g. `fr.html` for French.

{% /steps %}

When you generate a PDF, for example an invoice, pick your template under **Document template**. You can keep several, for example one per brand.

{% aside type="tip" %}
A typo in the data a template uses makes the PDF fail, so you'll notice right away. Check it in
the preview before uploading.
{% /aside %}
